§ `Regulation 4(2), (3): the period for the choice`

-- (2): three months starting on the date in the notice. Starting 15 January 2027 the
-- three months are 15 Jan - 14 Apr 2027 (convention F2).
#ASSERT (`regulation 4(2): the period for the choice where a notice has been issued` (YMD 2027 1 15))'s `the first day of the period for the choice` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 15
#ASSERT (`regulation 4(2): the period for the choice where a notice has been issued` (YMD 2027 1 15))'s `the last day of the period for the choice` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 14
-- (3)(a): starts on the LATER of claim and death. Claim 1 Mar, death 10 Feb: 1 Mar.
#ASSERT (`regulation 4(3): the period for the choice where the person chooses before any notice` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Feb, choice on 1 Mar`)'s `the first day of the period for the choice` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
-- Claim 1 Mar, death 10 Mar: 10 Mar.
#ASSERT (`regulation 4(3): the period for the choice where the person chooses before any notice` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Mar, choice on 10 Mar`)'s `the first day of the period for the choice` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 10
-- (3)(b): ends on the date the person makes the choice.
#ASSERT (`regulation 4(3): the period for the choice where the person chooses before any notice` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Feb, choice on 1 Mar`)'s `the last day of the period for the choice` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1

§ `Regulation 4(1): is the choice made within the period?`

-- Notice branch (2): both ends of 15 Jan - 14 Apr 2027 are inside, a day either side is outside.
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `notice 15 Jan 2027, choice on 15 Jan 2027` EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `notice 15 Jan 2027, choice on 14 Apr 2027` EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `notice 15 Jan 2027, choice on 15 Apr 2027` EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `notice 15 Jan 2027, choice on 14 Jan 2027` EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
-- No-notice branch (3): the period ends on the day of the choice, so a choice on or after
-- the start is in time, and one before the start (before the claim or before the death) is not.
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Feb, choice on 1 Mar` EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Feb, choice on 28 Feb` EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Mar, choice on 5 Mar` EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `no notice, claim 1 Mar and death 10 Mar, choice on 10 Mar` EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
-- Regulation 4(1) only applies to a person who falls within section 8(1): otherwise it does not cover the person.
#ASSERT `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `not within section 8(1)` EQUALS `regulation 4 does not cover the person`
#ASSERT `regulation 4(1): the period within which the person is to make the choice` `not within section 8(1)` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 4(4), (5): late choice`
`late choice, reasonable, lump sum repaid in full in the original currency` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS TRUE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS TRUE
`late choice, not reasonable` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS FALSE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS TRUE
`late choice, lump sum not repaid in full` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS TRUE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS TRUE
`late choice, lump sum repaid in another currency` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS TRUE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE
`late choice, reasonable, no lump sum was ever paid` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS TRUE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE
`late choice, not reasonable and no lump sum paid` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
    `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS FALSE
    `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
    `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS TRUE
    `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS TRUE

-- (4)(a) and (b) both required.
#ASSERT `regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `late choice, reasonable, lump sum repaid in full in the original currency`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `late choice, not reasonable`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `late choice, lump sum not repaid in full`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `late choice, lump sum repaid in another currency`)
-- No lump sum paid, so nothing to repay: (b) is met (fork F11). Asserted.
#ASSERT `regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `late choice, reasonable, no lump sum was ever paid`
-- The Secretary of State's judgment is still needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `late choice, not reasonable and no lump sum paid`)
-- (5): a late choice for a state pension reduces the lump sum to nil; otherwise it stands.
#ASSERT `regulation 4(5): the amount of the lump sum` 5000 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `regulation 4(5): the amount of the lump sum` 5000 FALSE EQUALS 5000

§ `Regulation 5: the manner of making the choice`

#ASSERT `regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE
-- (3): where the Secretary of State directs writing, writing is accepted ...
#ASSERT `regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE
-- (2)(b): telephone is accepted when no direction is given ...
#ASSERT `regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE
-- ... and refused when the Secretary of State has directed writing.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE)
-- Any manner the regulation does not list is not accepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` `in another manner` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 5(2) and (3): the manner is one the Regulations accept` `in another manner` TRUE)
-- Regulation 5 as a whole applies only to a person within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act.
#ASSERT `regulation 5: the choice is made in the manner required` TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `regulation 5: the choice is made in the manner required` TRUE `in another manner` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `regulation 5: the choice is made in the manner required` FALSE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

