§ `Regulation 6: may the choice be altered?`

-- All of (a) to (h) are required ("and" before (h)).
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, all conditions met`
-- (a) the person has not died; (b) an application is made.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, the person has died`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, no application`)
-- (c)(i): three months starting 15 Jan 2027 are 15 Jan - 14 Apr 2027.
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, applied on 15 Jan 2027, the day of the notification`
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, applied on 14 Apr 2027, the last day of three months`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, applied on 15 Apr 2027, a day late`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, applied on 14 Jan 2027, before the notification`)
-- (c)(ii): a longer period the Secretary of State considers reasonable.
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, applied on 15 Apr 2027 within a longer period to 30 Jun 2027`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, applied on 1 Jul 2027 after a longer period to 30 Jun 2027`)
-- (d): manner, as in regulation 5(2) and (3).
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration by telephone, no direction`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration by telephone, writing directed`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration in another manner`)
-- (e): an alteration to a state pension needs any lump sum repaid in full, in the original currency, within the (c) period.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, the lump sum not repaid in full`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, repaid in another currency`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, repaid on 15 Apr 2027, after the three months`)
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, repaid on 14 Apr 2027, the last day`
-- Fork F12: with a longer period, the repayment may be made up to the later end. Asserted.
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, applied and repaid on 15 Apr 2027 within a longer period to 30 Jun 2027`
-- No lump sum paid: nothing to repay (fork F11). Asserted.
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a state pension, no lump sum was paid`
-- (f): an alteration to a lump sum needs the pension paid to be LESS than the lump sum.
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a lump sum, pension paid is less (10000 against 12000)`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a lump sum, pension paid equals the lump sum`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a lump sum, pension paid is more`)
-- (e) is for an alteration to a state pension only; it does not bite on an alteration to a lump sum.
#ASSERT `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration to a lump sum, but the lump-sum repayment facts are false`
-- (g) and (h).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, an earlier alteration was made`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `alteration, treated as made under the 1987 Regulations`)

§ `Regulation 6(3): pension paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum`

#ASSERT `regulation 6(3): the state pension already paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum` `alteration to a lump sum, pension paid is less (10000 against 12000)`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(3): the state pension already paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum` `alteration to a lump sum, pension paid equals the lump sum`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 6(3): the state pension already paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum` `alteration to a state pension, all conditions met`)

§ `Regulation 7: suspending entitlement`

#ASSERT `regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` TRUE TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE
#ASSERT `regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` TRUE TRUE `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE
-- (3): writing is required where the Secretary of State directs it.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` TRUE TRUE `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE)
#ASSERT `regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` TRUE TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE
-- (1): only a person who has become entitled may opt to suspend; and they must give notice.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` FALSE TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` TRUE FALSE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` TRUE TRUE `in another manner` FALSE)

§ `Regulation 8: the date from which a suspension begins`

-- Option exercised on 10 March 2027: 28 days starting with 10 March run to 6 April
-- (10 March + 27 days; convention F1, fork F13).
#ASSERT `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` (YMD 2027 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 3 10)) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 10
#ASSERT `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` (YMD 2027 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 3 25)) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 25
#ASSERT `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` (YMD 2027 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 4 6)) EQUALS YMD 2027 4 6
-- One day after the 28th day, or before the day of exercise: not "in accordance with paragraph (2)", so (3) applies.
#ASSERT `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` (YMD 2027 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 4 7)) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 10
#ASSERT `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` (YMD 2027 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2027 3 9)) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 10
-- No date specified: (3).
#ASSERT `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` (YMD 2027 3 10) NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2027 3 10
#ASSERT `regulation 8(2): the specified date is one the Regulations allow` (YMD 2027 3 10) (YMD 2027 4 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 8(2): the specified date is one the Regulations allow` (YMD 2027 3 10) (YMD 2027 4 7))

§ `Regulation 9: cancelling a suspension`

-- Claim made on 15 March 2027: the past period reaches back 12 months, to 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `regulation 9(3): the earliest day to which a cancellation can reach back` (YMD 2027 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 14)
#ASSERT `regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 9 1) (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- A day before the twelve months, or reaching to the day of the claim itself, is outside.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 14) (YMD 2027 3 14))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 15))
-- (2): the suspension is cancelled by making a claim whilst the pension is suspended.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 14))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 14))
-- A period whose end is before its start is not a period.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 15) (YMD 2026 9 1) (YMD 2026 8 1))

§ `Regulation 10: the specified percentage`

-- Text: "one-ninth of 1%". Nine times one-ninth of 1% is 1%.
#ASSERT `regulation 10: the specified percentage for section 17(4) of the 2014 Act` TIMES 9 EQUALS 1%
-- One whole week at that percentage of 900 pounds is 1 pound.
#ASSERT `regulation 10: the weekly increase for the weeks counted` 1 900 EQUALS 1
-- Nine weeks at one-ninth of 1% make 1%: 1% of 200 is 2.
#ASSERT `regulation 10: the weekly increase for the weeks counted` 9 200 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `regulation 10: the weekly increase for the weeks counted` 0 900 EQUALS 0

§ `Regulation 11: days which do not count`

`day with a listed benefit` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS LIST `state pension credit`
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS EMPTY
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS FALSE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS FALSE

`day with the carer support payment, the newest listed benefit` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS LIST `the carer support payment component of carer support`
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS EMPTY
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS FALSE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS FALSE

`day with an increase received by a spouse` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS EMPTY
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS LIST `income support`
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS TRUE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS FALSE

`day with an increase received by a stranger` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS EMPTY
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS LIST `income support`
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS FALSE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS FALSE

`day with a spouse who received no increase` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS EMPTY
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS EMPTY
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS TRUE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS FALSE

`day as a prisoner` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS EMPTY
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS EMPTY
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS FALSE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS TRUE

`an ordinary day` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS EMPTY
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS EMPTY
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS FALSE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS FALSE

-- (2)(a): a listed benefit received by the deferred person on the day.
#ASSERT `regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day with a listed benefit`
#ASSERT `regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day with the carer support payment, the newest listed benefit`
-- (2)(b): an increase received by someone married to, in a civil partnership with, or living with the deferred person.
#ASSERT `regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day with an increase received by a spouse`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day with an increase received by a stranger`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day with a spouse who received no increase`)
-- (2)(c): the day on which the deferred person would not be paid because a prisoner.
#ASSERT `regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day as a prisoner`
-- No ground: the day counts.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `an ordinary day`)

-- (2)(c) is answered by regulations 2 and 3: a day on which regulation 2(1) says the
-- pension is not to be paid is a day that does not count. Composing the two modules:
`a person imprisoned on the day, for the composition test` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in the composition test`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS FALSE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS NOTHING

`imprisoned in the composition test` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`the day for the composition test` MEANS YMD 2027 5 5

`day facts fed from regulation 2(1)` MEANS DayFacts WITH
    `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS EMPTY
    `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS EMPTY
    `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS FALSE
    `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS `regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `the day for the composition test` `a person imprisoned on the day, for the composition test`

#ASSERT `regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `day facts fed from regulation 2(1)`

§ `Regulation 12: whole weeks counted`

`a deferral from 1 Jan to 31 Mar 2027` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
    `first day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 1
    `last day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 3 31

`a deferral of exactly one week` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
    `first day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 1
    `last day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 7

`a deferral of eight days` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
    `first day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 1
    `last day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 8

-- 1 Jan to 31 Mar 2027 is 31 + 28 + 31 = 90 days. 90 / 7 is 12 and 6/7: a part week, counted as a whole week: 13.
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral from 1 Jan to 31 Mar 2027` 0 EQUALS JUST 13
-- Six days discounted under regulation 11 leave 84 days: exactly 12 weeks.
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral from 1 Jan to 31 Mar 2027` 6 EQUALS JUST 12
-- Five days discounted leave 85 days: 12 weeks and a day, so 13.
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral from 1 Jan to 31 Mar 2027` 5 EQUALS JUST 13
-- Seven days make one week; eight days make a week and a part week: 2.
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral of exactly one week` 0 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral of eight days` 0 EQUALS JUST 2
-- Every day discounted leaves nothing: zero weeks.
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral of exactly one week` 7 EQUALS JUST 0
-- More days discounted than there are days in the period cannot be true: no answer.
#ASSERT `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `a deferral of exactly one week` 8 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 12A: modification where the rate changes during deferral`

`the deferral of 2027` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
    `first day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 1
    `last day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 12 31

-- (1): applies only if a non-uprating change falls inside the deferral period.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `the deferral of 2027` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `the deferral of 2027` (LIST YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `the deferral of 2027` (LIST YMD 2026 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `the deferral of 2027` (LIST YMD 2028 1 1))
#ASSERT `regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `the deferral of 2027` (LIST YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `the deferral of 2027` (LIST YMD 2027 12 31)
-- (3), (4): two changes cut the deferral into three periods.
#ASSERT count (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) EQUALS 3
-- First: from the start of the deferral to just before the first change.
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 0)'s `the first day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 0)'s `the last day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
-- Second: from the first change to just before the second.
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 1)'s `the first day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 1)'s `the last day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 5 31
-- Last: from the last change to the end of the deferral period.
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 2)'s `the first day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 6 1
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 3 1, YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 2)'s `the last day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 12 31
-- One change: two periods, the first ending the day before the change.
#ASSERT count (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 7 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (at (`regulation 12A(3) and (4): the modification periods from` (YMD 2027 1 1) (LIST YMD 2027 7 1) (YMD 2027 12 31)) 0)'s `the last day of the modification period` EQUALS YMD 2027 6 30
-- (2): the increment for a period is the specified percentage of the weekly rate: 10 weeks at 900 a week is 10 pounds.
#ASSERT `regulation 12A(2): the increment for a modification period` 10 900 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `regulation 12A(2): the increment for a modification period` 9 200 EQUALS 2
